{"resourceIdentifier":"4627","resourceName":"Trees for Livelihood in Madhya Pradesh, India","description":"The objective of the project is to increase the tree cover outside forest (ToF) areas through ARR activities on privately owned lands of farmers who belong to the local communities. Some plantation is also undertaken on common lands under the village or Gram Panchayat if the GP wishes to include the same. Apart from ARR activities, the project also works closely with the communities to address livelihoods. The project aims to secure the financial security of the local farming and other communities through planting of farmer friendly trees to support traditional crop-based agriculture systems and through support through supplementary community-based interventions. The PP implements the project through service providers, who work closely with farmers to assess willingness to participate in the project, engage them in project activities and undertake project activities with high levels of participation from the local communities. The project team on the ground are employed from the local community, and care is taken to ensure participation of women and other marginalized members of the community.","location":{"latitude":23.473319,"longitude":77.947997},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-09-12","endExclusive":"2023-10-13","endInclusive":"2023-10-12"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4627"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Madhya Pradesh"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Value Network Ventures PTE. LTD."},{"type":"string","value":"Singapore"},{"type":"string","value":"+91804249933"},{"type":"string","value":"sandeep@vnadvisory.net"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"